// api/tsconfig.json — the @vercel/node nearest-tsconfig pin (T052 follow-ups,
// W-3i resolution + W-3j emit).
//
// THE W-3i LESSON (deploy-triggered failure dpl_Ajr2KCQmT9axQGwDEcvpBkLFc4aV):
// after the W-3h discovery shim made Vercel FIND this function, the build's
// TypeScript typecheck still failed — @vercel/node resolves compiler options
// from the tsconfig.json NEAREST the function entry (walking up from
// api/router.ts), and with no tsconfig.json in api/ its default synthesis
// ran moduleResolution "nodenext". Under nodenext every extensionless
// relative import is an error (TS2835: "Relative import paths need explicit
// file extensions in ECMAScript imports... Did you mean './identity.js'?"),
// and the frozen services/api sources — plus this shim's own re-export —
// are written extensionless: the style the whole repo already typechecks
// green under. The TS2339/TS2322 errors in the build log were cascades —
// services/api's types collapsed first, so every consumer of them lost its
// types.
//
// THE W-3j LESSON (FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED on the exact function path
// /api/router — the static console served, the API plane dead): W-3i fixed
// the TYPECHECK but the emit stayed ESM ("module": "ESNext"). The platform
// build emitted a REAL tsc artifact whose entry carried
//   export { default } from '../deploy/vercel/api/router'
// verbatim — EXTENSIONLESS ESM specifiers, which Node cannot load:
// ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND under ESM resolution, and a SyntaxError ("Cannot
// use import statement outside a module") under CJS loading. The runtime
// loads CJS (the repo package.json has NO "type" field — CommonJS is the
// Node default), so the function must EMIT CommonJS. "moduleResolution":
// "Bundler" is NOT valid with "module": "CommonJS" (TS5095) — the pairing
// becomes "node" (node10): extensionless relative imports remain LEGAL
// under node10 (required — the frozen services/api sources and the deploy
// tree import extensionless; NEVER add extensions), so the W-3i
// typecheck law holds (no nodenext) while the emit becomes loadable.
// Under CommonJS the vitest-only TEST sources are EXCLUDED from this
// pin's include (they carry import.meta — legal in the vitest ESM
// runtime, illegal under a CommonJS compile: TS1343): tests are never
// part of the function's entry graph (the platform builds the entry +
// its import closure; vitest runs the tests). The node ambient types
// are pinned EXPLICITLY (typeRoots relative to THIS file = the repo
// root's node_modules/@types, the same provision the platform build
// makes — see .vercel/node/package-manifest.json; types ["node"]):
// runtime/http.ts (Buffer) and runtime/compose.ts (process) need them,
// and the W-3j proof gate compiles this pin from OUTSIDE the repo —
// the default typeRoots walk-up would start at the gate config's own
// directory and find nothing (TS2580/TS2688). Only "node" is visible
// under the pin (node_modules/@types holds nothing else), so the pin
// changes nothing about the repo's own typecheck.
//
// THE LAW (pinned by deploy/vercel/vercel.test.ts): NEVER add file
// extensions to the frozen services/api imports to satisfy a build tool —
// pin the resolution AND the emit instead. This file is the nearest
// tsconfig on the entry's walk-up path, so @vercel/node reads THESE
// options. Proof gate (W-3j): compile the entry with this config and
// REQUIRE the emitted file — if `require()` cannot load it, the emit is
// wrong.
{
  "extends": "../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "module": "CommonJS",
    "moduleResolution": "node",
    "typeRoots": ["../node_modules/@types"],
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["./**/*.ts", "../deploy/vercel/**/*.ts", "../services/api/**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": ["./**/*.test.ts", "../deploy/vercel/**/*.test.ts", "../services/api/**/*.test.ts"]
}
